# The product's default data dir (localDataDir(): <package>/../../data, i.e. this folder). It holds
# .master-key, settings.enc, session.enc (the portal refresh token), the SQLite desk, media, meeting
# recordings and unpacked native components. Ignored as a whole, not as a list of names, so a file
# the product starts writing tomorrow is never one `git add` away from a commit. The leading slash
# anchors it here: a source folder called `data` anywhere else stays tracked. Nothing under data/
# is tracked; if a file ever has to be, ignore `/data/*` instead and add a `!/data/<name>` line.
# See docs/internal/security-register.md, SR-19.
/data/
.cursor-artifacts/
apps/desktop/dist
apps/desktop/dist-*
apps/desktop/out
apps/desktop/host.cjs
apps/desktop/resources/web
apps/desktop/resources/renderer
apps/desktop/resources/drizzle
apps/desktop/branding/kemenkeu/
apps/desktop/branding/metranet/
apps/desktop/branding/_raw/
apps/desktop/logo.png
*.log
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.cursor/skills/verify-agentforge/evidence/**
!.cursor/skills/verify-agentforge/evidence/README.md
apps/web/tests/fixtures/edit/*.mp4
apps/web/tests/fixtures/edit/*.png
apps/desktop/resources/starters/*.mp4
apps/desktop/resources/starters/*.m4a
apps/desktop/resources/examples/videos/*.mp4
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
.claude/
_ref/

# Python bytecode from the mac build tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# isolated verification instance data (PORT=3100)
.verify-*/

# Webdev and review data directories. These hold `.master-key` and the desk SQLite file, so an
# untracked one is a `git add -A` away from a committed wrap key. `.webdev-data*` also covers the
# dated backups (`.webdev-data.bak-20260921/`). See docs/internal/security-register.md, SR-02.
.webdev-data*/
.dpsbuddy-review/

# Review-harness secrets and TLS material. `scripts/review-instance.ps1` writes review.env under
# $HOME and `scripts/review-proxy.mjs` generates its key pair there, but `--cert-dir` takes any
# path, so the repo refuses the file rather than trusting the flag.
review.env
*.pem
